    {
      "title": "Waymo pulls driverless taxis from freeways across the US after California ban",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/18/waymo-pulls-driverless-taxis-us-freeways",
      "description": "<p>The autonomous driving company suspended driverless taxi rides on US highways days after California banned the vehicles on its own freeways</p><p>Waymo has stopped offering driverless taxi rides on freeways across the US indefinitely. The Alphabet subsidiary pulled its vehicles from highways nationwide after <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/california\">California</a> banned them from freeways in response to recent traffic incidents.</p><p>Waymo had allowed riders to hail its robotaxis for freeway rides in the San Francisco Bay Area, Los Angeles, Phoenix, Miami and Austin. The California-based company offers rides on city streets in many other areas, including Las Vegas, Dallas and Denver. Those rides remain unaffected by suspended freeway service.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/18/waymo-pulls-driverless-taxis-us-freeways\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-18T22:05:49"
    }
